  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37215150",
      "title": "What Is HTTP & How Does It Work?",
      "lectureOrder": 224,
      "videoOrder": 208,
      "sourceHash": "5d3352be6a5cdb45f23b7b47ced5f7917c85aa05e3ce49fd3aa57e7603389325",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 3.84,
          "en": "So for certain kinds of apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.84,
          "end": 6.15,
          "en": "a backend server might be needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.15,
          "end": 8.16,
          "en": "And as mentioned in the previous lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.16,
          "end": 10.68,
          "en": "the communication between your Flutter app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.68,
          "end": 15.66,
          "en": "and such a backend server happens via HTTP.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.66,
          "end": 19.77,
          "en": "Now, in case you don't really know how HTTP works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.77,
          "end": 24.27,
          "en": "or what HTTP requests are, here's a quick overview.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.27,
          "end": 26.82,
          "en": "If you do know what HTTP is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.82,
          "end": 29.82,
          "en": "you can of course, skip this lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.82,
          "end": 33.03,
          "en": "So HTTP is that thing that in the end allows us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.03,
          "end": 35.49,
          "en": "to connect frontend and backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.49,
          "end": 38.01,
          "en": "It's in the end, a standardized protocol",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.01,
          "end": 41.07,
          "en": "that's used for communicating back and forth",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.07,
          "end": 43.86,
          "en": "between a frontend and a backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.86,
          "end": 45.57,
          "en": "And here's how that works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.57,
          "end": 47.16,
          "en": "It always starts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.16,
          "end": 51.06,
          "en": "with the frontend sending a so-called HTTP request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.06,
          "end": 55.53,
          "en": "to the backend if it wants something from the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.53,
          "end": 57.63,
          "en": "For example, in that shopping list app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.63,
          "end": 59.64,
          "en": "when a new item is added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.64,
          "end": 62.7,
          "en": "you might want to store that on a database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.7,
          "end": 64.59,
          "en": "that's managed by the backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.59,
          "end": 68.1,
          "en": "and therefore you would then send such a HTTP request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.1,
          "end": 71.58,
          "en": "from the frontend to the backend, telling the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.58,
          "end": 74.1,
          "en": "that the data should be stored.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.1,
          "end": 76.32,
          "en": "The backend then does its thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.32,
          "end": 79.05,
          "en": "it does the thing you want it to do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.05,
          "end": 82.41,
          "en": "and then ultimately, it will send back a response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.41,
          "end": 86.03999999999999,
          "en": "Though when I say it does the thing you want it to do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.03999999999999,
          "end": 89.13,
          "en": "that of course, implies that the backend is prepared",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.13,
          "end": 91.62,
          "en": "for the kind of work you want it to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.62,
          "end": 93.3,
          "en": "It's the code on the backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.3,
          "end": 95.72999999999999,
          "en": "the code with which the backend is written",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 95.72999999999999,
          "end": 99.06,
          "en": "that in the end defines what the backend is able to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.06,
          "end": 102.47999999999999,
          "en": "and which kind of HTTP requests it accepts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.47999999999999,
          "end": 104.55,
          "en": "In this course section, we're going",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.55,
          "end": 107.43,
          "en": "to use a dummy third party backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 107.43,
          "end": 110.82,
          "en": "a service that offers various backend services.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 110.82,
          "end": 113.7,
          "en": "Alternatively, you could also write your own backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 113.7,
          "end": 117.87,
          "en": "by using a programming language like Node.js, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 117.87,
          "end": 119.64,
          "en": "That's not what we'll do in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 119.64,
          "end": 121.26,
          "en": "but that is what you could do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 121.26,
          "end": 123.75,
          "en": "But ultimately, if you send the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 123.75,
          "end": 126.66,
          "en": "that's supported by the backend to the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 126.66,
          "end": 129.6,
          "en": "and the backend then processed that request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 129.6,
          "end": 131.82,
          "en": "and did whatever it had to do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 131.82,
          "end": 134.37,
          "en": "you get back such a response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 134.37,
          "end": 137.55,
          "en": "And both request and response are in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 137.55,
          "end": 140.34,
          "en": "standardized information packages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 140.34,
          "end": 143.97,
          "en": "This HTTP thing is a standardized protocol",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 143.97,
          "end": 146.07,
          "en": "that in the end defines how requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 146.07,
          "end": 147.81,
          "en": "and responses may look like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 147.81,
          "end": 151.71,
          "en": "For example, requests typically contain a URL,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 151.71,
          "end": 153.51,
          "en": "the address of the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 153.51,
          "end": 155.85,
          "en": "to which the request should be sent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 155.85,
          "end": 159.54,
          "en": "an HTTP method that can be picked up by the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 159.54,
          "end": 161.46,
          "en": "to perform different actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 161.46,
          "end": 164.64,
          "en": "for different requests with different methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 164.64,
          "end": 167.67000000000002,
          "en": "You could also add headers to your outgoing requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 167.67000000000002,
          "end": 169.82999999999998,
          "en": "which in the end is just a bunch of metadata",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 169.82999999999998,
          "end": 172.74,
          "en": "that could be picked up and used by the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 172.74,
          "end": 176.16,
          "en": "And you can also attach data to your outgoing requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 176.16,
          "end": 178.77,
          "en": "like for example, a new grocery item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 178.77,
          "end": 180.6,
          "en": "that should be stored in the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 180.6,
          "end": 182.19,
          "en": "That could be data attached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 182.19,
          "end": 185.403,
          "en": "to a request sent from the frontend to the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 186.69,
          "end": 189.69,
          "en": "Now when the backend then is done handling the request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 189.69,
          "end": 193.23,
          "en": "it will send back a response, which then in turn can be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 193.23,
          "end": 195.6,
          "en": "by the frontend to update the UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 195.6,
          "end": 200.4,
          "en": "and that response may include headers, so metadata again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 200.4,
          "end": 201.81,
          "en": "and also a body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 201.81,
          "end": 204.75,
          "en": "So data that is generated by the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 204.75,
          "end": 207.472,
          "en": "and that's then sent back from the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 207.472,
          "end": 209.94,
          "en": "to the frontend through the response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 209.94,
          "end": 213.93,
          "en": "So that's the first overview of how HTTP works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 213.93,
          "end": 215.82,
          "en": "If you wanna learn even more, you can search",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 215.82,
          "end": 219.51,
          "en": "for MDN HTTP to find the MDN Web Docs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 219.51,
          "end": 221.31,
          "en": "which is a great resource",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 221.31,
          "end": 223.86,
          "en": "for learning more about web development",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 223.86,
          "end": 225.45,
          "en": "and how the internet works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 225.45,
          "end": 226.86,
          "en": "And ultimately, this front",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 226.86,
          "end": 229.59,
          "en": "and backend thing is an internet thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 229.59,
          "end": 231.6,
          "en": "even though we're building a mobile app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 231.6,
          "end": 234.21,
          "en": "but we're using the internet for communication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 234.21,
          "end": 236.55,
          "en": "between the mobile app and the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 236.55,
          "end": 239.94,
          "en": "So here you can learn more about HTTP if you want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 239.94,
          "end": 242.58,
          "en": "And with that, you now got all the base knowledge you need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 242.58,
          "end": 246.21,
          "en": "to get started with this section where you will learn how",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 246.21,
          "end": 248.433,
          "en": "to connect your Flutter app to a backend.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
